    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** serving as our primary offensive catalysts. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) draws an elite matchup against the vulnerable Elmer Rodr\u00edguez; with a high-floor 5.31 xERA opponent and a projected #3 slot, he is the clear centerpiece for our production. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (78.04) benefits from the same favorable matchup against Seymour, providing the stability and upside required to keep our roto standings competitive. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) also warrants a high-leverage start, as his platoon advantage against Shane Baz drives his projection well into the strong-start tier, assuming he retains his assumed spot in the heart of the order.\n\nOur bench strategy today emphasizes discipline, as we prioritize game cap preservation by strictly adhering to the 40.0 efficiency floor. **Wade Meckler** (38.66) was the most difficult exclusion; while his projected #2 slot offers volume, the difficult matchup against Logan Gilbert combined with a park factor penalty pushed his efficiency just below our threshold. We are monitoring **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Coby Mayo** closely, as their scores are contingent on the finalization of their respective lineups. Any downward shift in their batting order will require a reassessment of their daily value.\n\nWhile we are bolstered by the core group, we remain cautious regarding the performance of **Nasim Nunez** (47.11). Although his speed is invaluable for our scarcity-driven strategy in stolen bases, the #9 spot in the order and a tough matchup against Jose Quintana\u2014despite our internal adjustments\u2014limits his offensive ceiling. We are currently navigating the absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose time on the IL or bench requires us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. With **Liam Hicks**, **Andy Pages**, and **Sam Antonacci** rounding out the lineup, we expect to maintain consistent floor output while banking on the elite ceiling of **Gunnar Henderson** to drive our category totals today.",
